# POSIX Fork Compliance Tests

This directory contains POSIX fork() compliance tests validating fork semantics.

## Source

Tests are based on the Open POSIX Test Suite (GPL-2):
https://github.com/emscripten-core/posixtestsuite

## Test Files

### POSIX Assertion Tests (1-1.c through 22-1.c)

| Test | Assertion |
|------|-----------|
| 1-1  | Fork concurrency (parent/child run concurrently) |
| 2-1  | Process state copied (environment, signals) |
| 3-1  | Child PID is unique |
| 4-1  | Child PPID equals parent PID |
| 5-1  | Child PID not active process group ID |
| 6-1  | Directory streams inherited |
| 7-1  | Message catalogs inherited |
| 8-1  | tms_utime/tms_stime reset to 0 |
| 9-1  | Alarm signals canceled in child |
| 10-1 | XSI semadj values cleared |
| 11-1 | File locks NOT inherited |
| 12-1 | Blocked signals inherited, pending cleared |
| 13-1 | Interval timers reset |
| 14-1 | Semaphores inherited |
| 15-1 | Memory locks NOT inherited |
| 16-1 | Memory mappings (COW semantics) |
| 17-1 | SCHED_RR inherited |
| 17-2 | SCHED_FIFO inherited |
| 18-1 | Per-process timers NOT inherited |
| 19-1 | Message queues inherited |
| 20-1 | Async I/O NOT inherited |
| 21-1 | Child has single thread |
| 22-1 | CPU-time clocks init to 0 |

### Custom Tests

| Test | Assertion |
|------|-----------|
| fork_fd_inherit | File descriptor inheritance |
| fork_fd_offset | FD offsets shared between parent/child |
| fork_return_values | Return values correct (0 child, PID parent) |
| fork_thread_replica | Thread ID replica in single-threaded child |
| fork_error | Error handling |
| fork_eagain | EAGAIN on resource exhaustion |
| fork_enomem | ENOMEM on memory exhaustion |

## Building

Tests use the testfrmw.h/testfrmw.c framework. Compile with:

    gcc -o test test.c -lpthread -lrt

## Exit Codes

- 0 (PTS_PASS): Test passed
- 1 (PTS_FAIL): Test failed
- 2 (PTS_UNRESOLVED): Could not determine result
- 4 (PTS_UNSUPPORTED): Feature not supported
- 5 (PTS_UNTESTED): Test skipped
- 77: Alternative skip code

## Fork Mode Testing

Tests can be run with different fork implementations:

    CYGWIN="fork_mode:legacy" ./test     # Traditional fork
    CYGWIN="fork_mode:rtlclone" ./test   # RtlCloneUserProcess fork

